      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تناظرا</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>They faced each other.</i> (K.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تناظرت الدَّارَانِ</span> (tropical:)  <i>The two houses faced
each other.</i> (M.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُورُنَا تَنَاظَرُ</span>, (S,) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتَنَاظَرُ</span>, [which is the original form,] (A,)
(tropical:)  <i>Our houses faced one another.</i> (S, A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَاوَضَا</span>.

